section('docs/architecture.md','## Native follow activity','''The `follow` command uses the existing physical action lane and movement owner. The single bundled-world tuning source is [base navigation](worlds/base/navigation.md#native-follow), re-exported through the native adapter for existing consumers. Following uses current visual evidence, bounded route updates and a hold/resume band. Losing perception, actions/locomotion capability, target viability or route support ends the activity honestly. Holding remains running. There is no hidden-position tracking, scent, stealth, sunset predicate or parallel movement writer.

Native and generated action labels use observer-specific descriptions. Short entity references, including nested navigation targets, resolve through the existing request-bound decoder. A global actor name is not available merely because the server knows it.''')
section('docs/architecture.md','## Private perception and evidence batches','''Visual acquisition records an observer-private `encounter` with observed modality and source/target provenance. Noticing something is not an outward act. Speech and physical effects retain their event-time audience rules. The fixed-position acquisition phase batches at most 128 new awareness entries through `mutateExperience`; this is an admission batch, not an observation cap. No evidence store or best-effort post-commit delivery was added.

Experience admission clones the caller's record and freezes that owned copy before insertion when the world is an immutable server-owned draft. Later owner edits still use drafts; external builder inputs are untouched. The former detached `current(rows)` evidence-freezing pass is removed. New events are sealed at native completion. Encounter-memory deduplication scans once per observer with new living contacts, not once per pair. The original patch-proven event-append lineage remains; a full-prefix-scan alternative was not retained.''')
section('docs/architecture.md','## Change-driven exposure and reaction intake','''The native post-movement frame captures current scalar entity fields without materializing the whole draft entity map and its action/status/agency subtrees. Immutable static objects reuse descriptors. Derived frames are keyed to exact committed snapshots; movement, removal, geometry, body/sense and perception-capability changes invalidate relevant results. Living and ordinary-object membership are reused independently: a moving person does not require rescanning unchanged static objects. Recomputed equal lists reuse the prior committed identity. An unchanged exposure with no outward-feature delta skips repeated acquisition sets and episode reconstruction.

The saved `perceptionFeatures` map is a coarse outward-feature baseline, not another knowledge store or generic sensory evaluator. Names of other actors use the knowledge owner's descriptions. Loss of perception clears live visibility and continuous recognition episodes; historical evidence remains. Moving sources still invalidate stationary observers. Main's installed status-effect semantics remain authoritative, including supported effects on non-actor objects; only inactive effects whose admission requires an actor skip inapplicable automatic checks.

`ActorWork` remains the coalesced scheduler. Repeated inspection of one frozen snapshot skips input reconstruction; diagnostic telemetry is not a cognition invalidator. At most 64 eligible schedule records are considered per pass with generation-aware acknowledgment. Main's current-evidence snapshot/coalescing behavior is preserved: old raw history is not a debt of queued model calls, and fixed cognition cooldowns/global thought intervals are not restored. `experiencesSince` remains available for ordered source access and maintenance without changing that policy. Raw sequence order is validated; safe existing arrays are stably ordered on upgrade without rewriting IDs or content. Lightweight per-mind signatures and source scans remain, rather than a fully mutation-fed regional index.

Startup and manual-save loading use the existing in-place upgrade path. Missing perception baselines and pending target/mode metadata receive conservative defaults; existing alternatives retain their mode. Malformed data is still rejected, and unrelated world identity, progress, accounting and evidence are not reset.''')
section('docs/architecture.md','## Cooperative native burst handling','''`advanceWorldWork` and synchronous `advanceWorld` share one deterministic transition. Checkpoints between actor work, status-effect groups, sensory candidates, acquisition groups and event sealing expose no candidate state. `native-step.ts` yields to the event loop after approximately eight milliseconds while `WorldService` keeps mutation ownership. Reads use the previous complete snapshot; commands cannot mutate a half-perceived world. No evidence is delayed into a later game tick or discarded to satisfy a budget.

Finalization, individual path queries, JSON encoding and database transactions can still block beyond that target. The real-server profiler records actual command latency, event-loop delays, simulated progress/debt and storage costs separately. Its dense SQLite case does not meet capacity or latency targets. A long-lived worker or asynchronous writer requires committed-only read isolation and measured benefit, not a second world authority. The existing long-callback suspension heuristic also remains a limitation during multi-second synchronous commits; counters expose excluded gaps, and nominal wall-time achieved speed must be reported rather than only admitted clock time.

The persistent `scripts/performance/profile-server.mjs` workload uses a disposable generated SQLite world, real native timer, SSE, and an independent client process with presence heartbeats. It bounds in-flight requests, reports rejections and skipped intervals, and disables paid providers. It does not qualify PostgreSQL, browser rendering, live cognition or long-session/multiplayer capacity.''')
edit('docs/architecture.md',lambda s:re.sub(r'The action slice advances current development saves to format 13 .*?earlier development worlds are rejected without mutation or migration\.', 'Action and perception state follow the active in-place upgrade policy; no per-feature world/save version or replacement data directory is required.',s,flags=re.S).replace('The retained architecture still has cold encounter/audience fan-out and bounded synchronous route preparation costs.', 'Remaining capacity limits include genuine dense acquisition/state construction, synchronous route preparation and persistence; private acquisition broadcasts have been removed.').replace('Changed queued work now retains actor cooldowns.', 'Changed queued work follows current actor eligibility.'))

section('docs/maintainers/performance.md','## Perception/evidence and burst delivery','''- [x] Remove private-acquisition audience amplification and batch through the existing experience owner; freeze owned record copies at insertion instead of materializing detached retained-history snapshots.
- [x] Read live perception scalars without whole-roster `current` copying; reuse living/object exposures independently and skip unchanged acquisition/episode reconstruction.
- [x] Preserve generic status-effect behavior while pruning inactive actor-only automatic conditions on non-actors; retain deterministic cooperative checkpoints through status phases.
- [x] Preserve main's current-evidence coalescing and diagnostic-independent ActorWork; do not restore fixed cognition cooldowns or a paid backlog-draining policy.
- [x] Record matched rebased-baseline/final native profiles plus real SQLite/HTTP/SSE workloads with a separate client and continuous presence. These are bounded observations, not population qualification; see [verification](../verification.md#rebased-action-and-perception-performance).
- [ ] Investigate the remaining dense first-commit cost through PF00/PF01: source/awareness construction, immutable state finalization, history encoding and SQLite transaction work must be attributed separately. Preserve individual evidence identity, privacy, revocation and atomicity. Do not yield a shared SQLite transaction to readers that could observe partial writes.
- [ ] Repeat full-server measurements with at least 1,000 successful commands, long mature history, 30-minute soaks, PostgreSQL, browser rendering and deterministic cognition/maintenance fixtures. Short 15-second phases have noisy tails and no live-model load.
- [ ] Address multi-second synchronous work interacting with the existing callback-gap suspension heuristic before claiming dense-world clock fidelity. Do not infer a new absence policy from CPU guesses or hide excluded time; remove blocking or qualify independent liveness evidence under PF10.
- [ ] Qualify the remaining per-mind/source signature walks and active-evidence array copy-on-write cost before introducing regional indexes or paged state. No witness dropping, changed perception rules, or guessed capacity promises.

### Residual capture and dense-scene gate

The earlier scalar-capture timeout investigation is superseded by the completed matched warm/cold capture measurements and preserved native digests. Source capture no longer calls `current` on the entire entity roster. The full-patch-elimination experiment was reverted: modest inconsistent benefit did not justify a retained-event prefix scan. Remaining dense-state/storage work stays open above; moving work to a worker alone does not reduce legitimate output volume.''')
# Replace the now-obsolete broad fan-out diagnosis, retaining the capacity qualification task.
edit('docs/maintainers/performance.md',lambda s:s.replace('Qualify and reduce first-exposure encounter/event/awareness fan-out before a population-scale claim. The existing mixed native scenario still exhibits a large cold maximum;', 'Qualify genuine dense acquisition and downstream storage before a population-scale claim. Accidental observer broadcast amplification is fixed;').replace('seal newly owned evidence at the final native phase','freeze owned evidence at admission').replace('Consume the ordered new-evidence tail; bound schedule reads and preserve newer dirty generations.', 'Preserve current-evidence coalescing; bound schedule reads and preserve newer dirty generations.'))
section('docs/performance.md','## Rebased acquisition and full-server measurement','''Keep native output correctness separate from implementation cost. Reuse unchanged observer/source relationships, freeze owned experience copies at insertion, and avoid whole-roster draft snapshots. Preserve generic status and knowledge semantics; never exchange actor-private evidence for a shared knowledge cache. Existing authoritative owners and deterministic transition order remain unchanged.

Measure the native kernel and actual server separately using the existing native profiler and the [bounded server workload](maintainers/performance-profiling.md#full-server-workload). Real-time debt, successful/rejected commands, SSE/projection, persistence, event-loop delay and excluded clock gaps all matter. Cold acquisition occurs after normal server bootstrap; native cold profiles remain a separate cache-start workload. Phase maxima labeled cumulative are not per-phase latency percentiles. Implementation, evidence and residual gates remain in [PF](maintainers/performance.md#perceptionevidence-and-burst-delivery) and [Verification](verification.md#rebased-action-and-perception-performance).''')
section('docs/maintainers/performance-profiling.md','## Full-server workload','''Run a generated, disposable scene through the real server timer, SQLite, SSE and a separate-process client:

```sh
pnpm run build
node --import tsx scripts/performance/profile-server.mjs scripts/performance/scenarios/mixed.json /tmp/openlegend-server-report.json 15 1,3,8
```

The output path must be new. The duration accepts 5–60 seconds per phase; supported requested speeds are 1, 3 and 8. Setup creates a private temporary data directory, populates a generated scenario with the timer disabled, then restarts the same world for actual timed measurement. User-save inputs are rejected. The profiler removes only its own temporary directory and disables all paid dispatch. It is not a PostgreSQL, browser, hosted-player or live-cognition benchmark.

A separate process reads state at 4 Hz, submits short move/cancel intentions at 2 Hz, consumes SSE, and sends presence heartbeats every 3 seconds. Each request lane has bounded concurrency. The report separates rejected requests, errors, request-scheduling lateness and skipped intervals from successful command latency; it cannot silently count an ungenerated request as success. SSE reports bytes/chunks, not browser render completion.

The first phase includes acquisition after ordinary bootstrap. Later phases reuse the evolving world and start at their recorded simulation time; do not describe these as independent identical fresh worlds. Before/after runs use the same host and scripted load, but wall-timed physics can diverge and small samples have noisy tails. Native fixed-step digest comparisons are separate evidence.

Report nominal elapsed-time achieved speed together with admitted/requested clock counters, pending debt and excluded gaps. Pending debt excludes elapsed wall time that an in-progress timer operation has not yet admitted. Existing >2-second callback-gap detection can misclassify long synchronous persistence as absence; the dense case does not qualify that boundary. Metric totals/counts are phase deltas, while `cumulativeMaxMs` is explicitly since startup. Keep initial presence-expiry runs separate from continuous-presence capacity evidence.

Long soaks, larger successful-command samples, genuine multiple players, slow consumers, PostgreSQL, browser rendering and no-network cognition/maintenance fixtures remain PF00/PF11 acceptance work.''')

